{"timestamp":"2026-09-10T13:46:51.470Z","ordinal":36276,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_0873a68aa02aff8f016aa2b4a9380c8198a05a9fa06f4b7cbc","status":"completed","call_id":"call_tHKtm09qEfwnVqb6GQYK1eA0","name":"exec","input":"const patch = \"*** Begin Patch\\n*** Update File: /Users/thomi/Projects/entire-brain/internal/tui/quality_review.go\\n@@\\n-\\tfooterText := \\\"↑↓/jk scroll · c context · p details · x skip · q quit · ? help\\\"\\n+\\tfooterText := \\\"↑↓ scroll · ←→ choose · Enter · y/n/u · c context · x skip · q quit · ? help\\\"\\n@@\\n-\\t\\tfooter += \\\"\\\\n\\\" + m.theme.dimStyle().Render(\\\"Your job is to judge the highlighted statement, not the transcript. Answer y/n/u three times, optionally add a note, then confirm. No panel answer is preselected.\\\")\\n+\\t\\tfooter += \\\"\\\\n\\\" + m.theme.dimStyle().Render(\\\"Judge the highlighted statement, not the transcript. Up/down scroll; left/right choose an answer; Enter submits it; p toggles extra judge explanations. No panel answer is preselected.\\\")\\n@@\\n \\tcase qualityReviewAuthority:\\n-\\t\\treturn \\\"2/3 · User endorsed?\\\"\\n+\\t\\treturn \\\"2/3 · Said or approved?\\\"\\n@@\\n \\tcase qualityReviewAuthority:\\n-\\t\\treturn m.answerPrompt(\\\"Did the user state or explicitly approve this?\\\")\\n+\\t\\treturn m.answerPrompt(\\\"Did the user say this themselves, or explicitly approve it?\\\")\\n*** Update File: /Users/thomi/Projects/entire-brain/internal/cli/distill_quality_adjudicate_v1.go\\n@@\\n-\\t\\tauthority, quit, err := readDistillQualityTernaryChoiceV1(reader, output, \\\"Did the user state or explicitly approve this? [y/n/u/q]: \\\")\\n+\\t\\tauthority, quit, err := readDistillQualityTernaryChoiceV1(reader, output, \\\"Did the user say this themselves, or explicitly approve it? [y/n/u/q]: \\\")\\n*** Update File: /Users/thomi/Projects/entire-brain/internal/cli/distill_quality_report_v1.go\\n@@\\n-\\tout.WriteString(\\\"The default is a balanced 20-item calibration batch in a full-screen terminal workspace. It isolates the exact statement the automatic filter judged, shows that statement first, and keeps surrounding conversation hidden unless you press `c`. Copilot, Cursor, and Claude appear as compact advisory answers with no human choice preselected. For each statement, answer whether it is potential long-term project knowledge, whether it has human authority, and whether its source is safe; use `y`, `n`, or `u`. Scroll with `j`/`k` or the arrow keys, use `p` for extra judge explanations, `x` to skip, `q` to stop, and `?` for help. A decision is written only after the confirmation step; every confirmed answer is saved immediately and the same command resumes without repeating it. Use `--plain` for the line-oriented accessibility or non-TTY fallback.\\\\n\\\\n\\\")\\n+\\tout.WriteString(\\\"The default is a balanced 20-item calibration batch in a full-screen terminal workspace. It isolates the exact statement the automatic filter judged, shows that statement first, and keeps surrounding conversation hidden unless you press `c`. Copilot, Cursor, and Claude appear as compact advisory answers with no human choice preselected. For each statement, answer whether it should be remembered for future project work, whether the user said or explicitly approved it, and whether it is safe evidence rather than one-off or generated material. Use `y`, `n`, or `u` directly, or choose with left/right and submit with Enter. Up/down scrolls; `p` shows extra judge explanations, `x` skips, `q` stops, and `?` opens help. A decision is written only after the confirmation step; every confirmed answer is saved immediately and the same command resumes without repeating it. Use `--plain` for the line-oriented accessibility or non-TTY fallback.\\\\n\\\\n\\\")\\n*** Update File: /Users/thomi/Projects/entire-brain/docs/candidate_distillation_plan.md\\n@@\\n-information are optional views. The reviewer explicitly answers long-term\\n-value, human authority, and source safety with `y`, `n`, or `u`; no answer is\\n-prefilled from the panel. A separate confirmation step is the only save action.\\n+information are optional views. The reviewer explicitly answers whether the\\n+statement should be remembered for future work, whether the user said or\\n+explicitly approved it, and whether it is safe evidence rather than one-off or\\n+generated material. Answers may be entered with `y`, `n`, or `u`, or selected\\n+with left/right and submitted with Enter; up/down scrolls the detail. No answer\\n+is prefilled from the panel. A separate confirmation step is the only save action.\\n*** End Patch\";\ntext(await tools.apply_patch(patch));","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a08b8a-def0-7e63-a99f-44a2793ce053"}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-09-10T13:46:51.513Z","ordinal":36277,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a0200a-63d8-7b21-adef-c3850aecebf7","turn_id":"01a08b8a-def0-7e63-a99f-44a2793ce053","item":{"type":"FileChange","id":"exec-b92a4a82-1ace-40a2-a541-d548e51376d7","changes":{"/Users/thomi/Projects/entire-brain/internal/tui/quality_review.go":{"type":"update","unified_diff":"@@ -485,3 +485,3 @@\n \t}\n-\tfooterText := \"↑↓/jk scroll · c context · p details · x skip · q quit · ? help\"\n+\tfooterText := \"↑↓ scroll · ←→ choose · Enter · y/n/u · c context · x skip · q quit · ? help\"\n \tif m.stage == qualityReviewRationaleEdit {\n@@ -491,3 +491,3 @@\n \tif m.help {\n-\t\tfooter += \"\\n\" + m.theme.dimStyle().Render(\"Your job is to judge the highlighted statement, not the transcript. Answer y/n/u three times, optionally add a note, then confirm. No panel answer is preselected.\")\n+\t\tfooter += \"\\n\" + m.theme.dimStyle().Render(\"Judge the highlighted statement, not the transcript. Up/down scroll; left/right choose an answer; Enter submits it; p toggles extra judge explanations. No panel answer is preselected.\")\n \t}\n@@ -713,3 +713,3 @@\n \tcase qualityReviewAuthority:\n-\t\treturn \"2/3 · User endorsed?\"\n+\t\treturn \"2/3 · Said or approved?\"\n \tcase qualityReviewSafety:\n@@ -730,3 +730,3 @@\n \tcase qualityReviewAuthority:\n-\t\treturn m.answerPrompt(\"Did the user state or explicitly approve this?\")\n+\t\treturn m.answerPrompt(\"Did the user say this themselves, or explicitly approve it?\")\n \tcase qualityReviewSafety:\n","move_path":null},"/Users/thomi/Projects/entire-brain/internal/cli/distill_quality_report_v1.go":{"type":"update","unified_diff":"@@ -112,3 +112,3 @@\n \tout.WriteString(\"```\\n\\n\")\n-\tout.WriteString(\"The default is a balanced 20-item calibration batch in a full-screen terminal workspace. It isolates the exact statement the automatic filter judged, shows that statement first, and keeps surrounding conversation hidden unless you press `c`. Copilot, Cursor, and Claude appear as compact advisory answers with no human choice preselected. For each statement, answer whether it is potential long-term project knowledge, whether it has human authority, and whether its source is safe; use `y`, `n`, or `u`. Scroll with `j`/`k` or the arrow keys, use `p` for extra judge explanations, `x` to skip, `q` to stop, and `?` for help. A decision is written only after the confirmation step; every confirmed answer is saved immediately and the same command resumes without repeating it. Use `--plain` for the line-oriented accessibility or non-TTY fallback.\\n\\n\")\n+\tout.WriteString(\"The default is a balanced 20-item calibration batch in a full-screen terminal workspace. It isolates the exact statement the automatic filter judged, shows that statement first, and keeps surrounding conversation hidden unless you press `c`. Copilot, Cursor, and Claude appear as compact advisory answers with no human choice preselected. For each statement, answer whether it should be remembered for future project work, whether the user said or explicitly approved it, and whether it is safe evidence rather than one-off or generated material. Use `y`, `n`, or `u` directly, or choose with left/right and submit with Enter. Up/down scrolls; `p` shows extra judge explanations, `x` skips, `q` stops, and `?` opens help. A decision is written only after the confirmation step; every confirmed answer is saved immediately and the same command resumes without repeating it. Use `--plain` for the line-oriented accessibility or non-TTY fallback.\\n\\n\")\n \tfmt.Fprintf(&out, \"Run `%s` contains %d packets: %d critical, %d with judge disagreement, %d with invalid judge output, and %d with missing judges. These are attention-routing counts, not human error labels.\\n\\n\", manifest.RunID, result.Packets, result.Critical, result.Disagreement, result.Invalid, result.MissingJudges)\n","move_path":null},"/Users/thomi/Projects/entire-brain/internal/cli/distill_quality_adjudicate_v1.go":{"type":"update","unified_diff":"@@ -330,3 +330,3 @@\n \t\t}\n-\t\tauthority, quit, err := readDistillQualityTernaryChoiceV1(reader, output, \"Did the user state or explicitly approve this? [y/n/u/q]: \")\n+\t\tauthority, quit, err := readDistillQualityTernaryChoiceV1(reader, output, \"Did the user say this themselves, or explicitly approve it? [y/n/u/q]: \")\n \t\tif err != nil {\n","move_path":null},"/Users/thomi/Projects/entire-brain/docs/candidate_distillation_plan.md":{"type":"update","unified_diff":"@@ -172,5 +172,8 @@\n Cursor, and Claude recommendations; detailed rationales and local source\n-information are optional views. The reviewer explicitly answers long-term\n-value, human authority, and source safety with `y`, `n`, or `u`; no answer is\n-prefilled from the panel. A separate confirmation step is the only save action.\n+information are optional views. The reviewer explicitly answers whether the\n+statement should be remembered for future work, whether the user said or\n+explicitly approved it, and whether it is safe evidence rather than one-off or\n+generated material. Answers may be entered with `y`, `n`, or `u`, or selected\n+with left/right and submitted with Enter; up/down scrolls the detail. No answer\n+is prefilled from the panel. A separate confirmation step is the only save action.\n `x` skips without writing, `q` discards only the current partial decision, and\n","move_path":null}},"status":"completed","stdout":"Success. Updated the following files:\nM /Users/thomi/Projects/entire-brain/internal/tui/quality_review.go\nM /Users/thomi/Projects/entire-brain/internal/cli/distill_quality_adjudicate_v1.go\nM /Users/thomi/Projects/entire-brain/internal/cli/distill_quality_report_v1.go\nM /Users/thomi/Projects/entire-brain/docs/candidate_distillation_plan.md\n","stderr":""},"started_at_ms":1789048011511,"completed_at_ms":1789048011513}}
