{"timestamp":"2026-09-10T17:17:55.216Z","ordinal":36397,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"function_call","id":"fc_0873a68aa02aff8f016aa2e6429a888198828181408b83e712","name":"list_agents","namespace":"collaboration","arguments":"{}","call_id":"call_zUhkSmnOsYZWyg3aFrO7fuhn","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a08c52-627e-72c2-ad24-e4d4de487a71"}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-09-10T17:17:55.290Z","ordinal":36398,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"function_call_output","id":"fco_01a08c53-76da-76c2-a685-94a57fe8dba6","call_id":"call_zUhkSmnOsYZWyg3aFrO7fuhn","output":"{\"agents\":[{\"agent_name\":\"/root\",\"agent_status\":\"running\"},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/focus_packet_audit\",\"agent_status\":{\"completed\":\"Read-only audit complete on `feat/candidate-distillation-quality-gate`.\\n\\nThe bundle contains exactly 719 packets: 219 admitted and 500 filtered.\\n\\nDeterministic extraction that works for all 719:\\n\\n1. Concatenate `payload.fragments[].text` in array order. Do not parse fragments independently; 77 packets split in the middle of a line.\\n2. Scan only line-start markers `user: ` and `assistant: `.\\n3. Use metadata to select the trigger:\\n   - Admitted packets: the sole `user` segment is the focus; every assistant segment is surrounding context.\\n   - Filtered packets: the sole segment matching `item.text.roles[0]` is the focus; context is empty.\\n4. Preserve the selected turn verbatim after the role prefix. Do not sentence-summarize: several “focus turns” contain multiple claims or pasted documents, and summarizing would discard evidence.\\n\\nObserved role shapes:\\n\\n| Packet type | Shape | Count |\\n|---|---:|---:|\\n| Admitted | assistant → user → assistant | 195 |\\n| Admitted | user → assistant | 15 |\\n| Admitted | assistant → user | 5 |\\n| Admitted | user only | 4 |\\n| Filtered user | user only | 321 |\\n| Filtered assistant | assistant only | 179 |\\n\\nAll 719 have exactly one selectable focus segment, begin with a valid role marker, and have `evidence_truncated=false`. No unexpected role-like line prefixes appeared. Focus lengths range from 2 characters (`d'`) to 32,383 characters; the largest admitted focus is 22,245 characters.\\n\\nImportant adversarial cases to fail closed on:\\n\\n- Multiple occurrences of the metadata trigger role: metadata does not identify which occurrence is authoritative.\\n- Content containing a line beginning `user: ` or `assistant: `: this is indistinguishable from a real turn boundary using the sealed packet alone.\\n- Filtered packets containing extra role segments.\\n- `evidence_truncated=true`: no exact focus can be claimed.\\n\\nThe TUI’s garbling is real: it currently shows merged raw evidence and only says `Candidate filter: ADMITTED`; it never identifies the actual candidate statement. Render separate sections:\\n\\n```text\\nFocus\\n  user: <one selected trigger turn>\\n\\nSurrounding context (not the candidate)\\n  assistant: <adjacent context>\\n```\\n\\nFor acceptance cues, the plan permits showing the preceding assistant proposal alongside the user’s acceptance, but that is a two-turn focus exchange—not literally one statement.\"}},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/quality_tui_impl\",\"agent_status\":{\"completed\":\"Implemented the full-screen quality-review TUI in:\\n\\n- [quality_review.go](/Users/thomi/Projects/entire-brain/internal/tui/quality_review.go)\\n- [quality_review_test.go](/Users/thomi/Projects/entire-brain/internal/tui/quality_review_test.go)\\n\\nAPI:\\n\\n```go\\nRunQualityReview(input, output, theme, review, save) (QualityReviewResult, error)\\n```\\n\\nSave callback receives `itemID, admission, authority, safety, rationale` strings; answers are `yes/no/unclear`. Includes progress/result models, wide/narrow layout, scrolling/resizing, explicit confirmation-only saves, visible errors, skip/quit safety, and rationale text editing.\\n\\nValidation: `go test ./internal/tui` passes.\"}},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/tui_ux_contract\",\"agent_status\":{\"completed\":\"Read-only findings and a concrete UX contract for `/root`:\\n\\nCurrent behavior is a line-oriented prompt in [`distill_quality_adjudicate_v1.go`](/Users/thomi/Projects/entire-brain/internal/cli/distill_quality_adjudicate_v1.go:384). It dumps all evidence, every judge rationale/raw JSON score, then asks sequential `y/n/u` questions. That explains the unreadable output. Existing dashboard patterns already provide Bubble Tea, viewport scrolling, lipgloss themes, resize handling, `?` help, and non-TTY routing in [`internal/tui`](/Users/thomi/Projects/entire-brain/internal/tui) and [`dash.go`](/Users/thomi/Projects/entire-brain/internal/cli/dash.go:547).\\n\\nRecommended screen contract:\\n\\n```text\\n┌─ Distill quality adjudication ───────────────────────────────┐\\n│ reviewer: thomi   queue: calibration   item 1/20             │\\n│ progress: 4/37 reviewed   remaining: 33   [CRITICAL]         │\\n├─ Candidate ───────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\\n│ ADMITTED · stratum: ...                                      │\\n│ “short candidate statement / kind”                           │\\n├─ Evidence ─────────────────────────────── scroll: 1/8 ──────┤\\n│ span-001                                                      │\\n│ wrapped evidence text, preserving fragment boundaries         │\\n│ span-002                                                      │\\n│ wrapped evidence text                                        │\\n├─ Advisory panel ──────────────────────────────────────────────┤\\n│ judge       admission   authority   safety     state           │\\n│ Claude      CRITICAL    PASS        CONCERN    completed       │\\n│ Copilot     ...                                             │\\n│ Cursor      ...                                             │\\n│ [r] show selected judge rationale/details                    │\\n├─ Decision ────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\\n│ Admission:  [Y] admit  [N] reject  [U] unclear  [S] skip       │\\n│ Authority: [Y] adequate [N] inadequate [U] unclear            │\\n│ Safety:    [Y] safe     [N] unsafe     [U] unclear            │\\n│ Rationale: type here (optional)                              │\\n├───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\\n│ ↑↓/j k scroll  v evidence  r rationale  enter save  n next  │\\n│ s skip  q quit  ? help                                       │\\n└───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\\n```\\n\\n- Keep the candidate/admission, authority, and safety concepts aligned with the existing persistence model: `accept`, `reject`, or `needs_review`; dimensions become proof labels.\\n- Advisory judge output is input only. Render compact labels by default; hide raw JSON and long rationales behind `r`/detail viewport.\\n- Evidence must be wrapped and fragment-labelled. `v` toggles full evidence; otherwise use a scrollable viewport rather than head/tail dumping.\\n- Never rely on color alone: display `PASS`, `CONCERN`, `CRITICAL`, `ABSTAIN`, and `INVALID` text labels.\\n\\nDecision and save semantics:\\n\\n- State machine: `review item → admission → authority → safety → rationale → confirm/save`.\\n- `y/n/u` should work both as direct keys and via clearly labelled buttons/help.\\n- `s` skips without creating a record.\\n- `v` toggles full evidence without changing state.\\n- `q`/Ctrl-C exits immediately. If a partially entered item is unsaved, discard it and report “not saved”; previously completed records remain.\\n- Save atomically and immediately after final confirmation, then advance to the next item. Existing tests establish immediate persistence/resume and mode `0600` ([`distill_quality_adjudicate_v1_test.go`](/Users/thomi/Projects/entire-brain/internal/cli/distill_quality_adjudicate_v1_test.go:11)).\\n- On completion, show a concise summary and output path; do not repeat all packet data.\\n\\nResize/scroll:\\n\\n- At wide terminals (roughly ≥100 columns), use a two-pane layout: evidence left/main and advisory/details right.\\n- Below that, stack panes vertically. Below a minimum usable width/height, keep the same sections but viewport-scroll them; never truncate silently.\\n- Recompute wrapped lines and viewport dimensions on every `WindowSizeMsg`, preserving the current logical fragment/line where possible.\\n- Evidence and advisory details should have independent scroll positions; global `↑/↓`, PageUp/PageDown, Home/End should scroll the focused viewport.\\n- Keep footer/help visible when possible; `?` expands the existing Bubble Tea help model.\\n\\nTTY/accessibility fallback:\\n\\n- Only start Bubble Tea when both input and output are terminals, matching `dash.go`’s `commandOutputIsTTY` convention.\\n- Non-TTY should retain a deterministic plain-text mode (the current prompt flow is a reasonable compatibility fallback), with no ANSI/alternate-screen assumptions. Consider an explicit `--plain` flag if the implementation needs to distinguish forced plain mode.\\n- Honor `NO_COLOR`/dumb terminals and provide ASCII alternatives for box-drawing/status glyphs. All statuses and actions must remain understandable without color or Unicode.\\n- Never emit an interactive TUI into a pipe; either run the plain flow or return an actionable “requires a TTY; use --plain” error.\\n\\nBounded tests:\\n\\n- Pure rendering test at wide and narrow dimensions: assert candidate, evidence fragment IDs, compact judge labels, progress, and action help are present; assert raw JSON is absent from the default view.\\n- Key/state-machine test: admission → authority → safety → rationale → save produces exactly one valid record and advances.\\n- `v` toggles full evidence; evidence viewport scrolls and survives resize without panic.\\n- `s` does not write; `q` exits and does not write a partial record; prior records remain.\\n- Resize breakpoint test verifies wide split versus narrow stacked layout.\\n- Accessibility test with ASCII/no-color mode asserts semantic status words remain visible.\\n- Preserve existing integration tests for save/resume, repeated evidence view, stale advisory rejection, and deterministic queue selection rather than replacing them.\"}}]}","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a08c52-627e-72c2-ad24-e4d4de487a71"}}}
